-- HM CORRECTIVE ACTIONS — canonical default change (simulation batch 7).
--
-- THE DEFECT: correctiveActions.manage shipped in the audit-readiness
-- build (20260915021000) for administrator / compliance_admin /
-- program_manager, but the house_manager pack never received it — in
-- src/data/permissions.ts, in the regenerated seed
-- (20260915024000_integrated_permissions.sql), or in live agency_roles
-- copies. The house manager owns QA follow-up at their home, yet could
-- only VIEW corrective actions: no role at the house could start one,
-- and QA Review offered no creation path at all. The simulation's HM
-- and the Audit-center surface both dead-ended on this key.
--
-- THE CURE (the repo's seed-refresh pattern, plus one deliberate flip):
--  1. role_permission_matrix is refreshed with the canonical maps
--     generated from src/data/permissions.ts (HM now true).
--  2. The standard merge fills MISSING keys into role_templates and
--     agency_roles; existing choices win for every other key.
--  3. For THIS key on house_manager only, the stored value is flipped
--     to the new canonical default even where present: the false in
--     every existing copy was written by the seed itself, never chosen
--     through Roles & access in response to this capability (the UI
--     offered the toggle, but the capability it gates — house-level QA
--     follow-up — is the defect being repaired). An agency that wants
--     house managers out of corrective actions can turn the key back
--     off in Roles & access after this migration.
